l like an accusation, creating an anxious mood.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;The mood is proud because underlining is neat.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L02_R_Q21</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The house held its breath until the key turned. How does the figurative language affect mood?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfeedback><defaultgrade>1.0000000</defaultgrade><penalty>0.3333333</penalty><single>true</single><shuffleanswers>true</shuffleanswers><answernumbering>none</answernumbering><showstandardinstruction>1</showstandardinstruction><correctfeedback format="html"><text /></correctfeedback><partiallycorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></partiallycorrectfeedback><incorrectfeedback format="html"><text /></incorrectfeedback><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates comedy because houses breathe.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates boredom because keys are common.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="0.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;It creates pride because keys shine.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer><answer fraction="100.0" format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Personification makes the house seem tense and expectant until someone arrives and turns the key.&lt;/p&gt;</text><feedback format="html"><text /></feedback></answer></question><question type="multichoice"><name><text>CW_U04_L02_R_Q22</text></name><questiontext format="html"><text>&lt;p&gt;Poem: The creek whispered secrets under a roof of leaves. Which analysis is strongest?&lt;/p&gt;</text></questiontext><generalfeedback format="html"><text /></generalfe